{"word": "leader", "source": "freedictionaryapi", "data": {"word": "leader", "entries": [{"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "noun", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈliː.də(ɹ)/", "tags": ["UK"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈli.dɚ/", "tags": ["Canada", "US"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "[ˈli.ɾɚ]", "tags": ["Canada", "US"]}], "forms": [{"word": "leaders", "tags": ["plural"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "Any person who leads or directs.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "In an era when political leaders promise deliverance from decline through America’s purported preeminence in scientific research, the news that science is in deep trouble in the United States has been as unwelcome as a diagnosis of leukemia following the loss of health insurance.", "reference": "2012 January 25, Philip E. Mirowski, “Harms to Health from the Pursuit of Profits”, in American Scientist, volume 100, number 1, archived from the original on 04 Apr 2012, page 87:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": [{"definition": "One who goes first.", "tags": [], "examples": ["Follow the leader."], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "One having authority to direct.", "tags": [], "examples": ["We elected her team leader."], "quotes": [{"text": "America needs not only an administrator, but a leader - a pathfinder, a blazer of the trail to the high road that will avoid the bottomless morass of crass materialism that has engulfed so many of the great civilizations of the past.", "reference": "1928, Franklin D. Roosevelt, The Happy Warrior Alfred E. Smith, Houghton Mifflin, →OCLC, →OL, page 40:"}, {"text": "On the other hand, I must think of Korea and, particularly, of the three million enslaved Koreans in the North. My obligation as a leader of the Korean people is to achieve unification of our country by peaceful means if possible but by force if necessary.", "r